 "summary": "Host only; nothing flashed, run or written on the phone. The payload kernel (artifacts/nat-020/build-003/payload.bin) carries a loader hook: _loader_stub_slot at VA 0xfffffff00743c7f0 (magic XNULDRST, stub PA, checkpoint, PA-VA), five assembly checkpoints in start.s (the fifth is the first point with the MMU on), 23 C checkpoints in arm_init, an early-exception report that hands ESR/ELR/FAR/LR/SP and the 1.5 MiB loader_log to the stub, and loader_return() from the panic paths. Decoded from the real bytes, cross-checked with capstone. Not established: any behaviour on hardware, the loader's slot fill (NAT-030), what the kernel's quiesce calls do on this SoC, whether kprintf reaches loader_log here, and the S-Boot SEC_UPLOAD protocol.",
